From 87872d205ae952873da68196e841bf976c11ffce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:45:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(market-sensitivity): exact previews, editable reference
 fields, complete live log, working filters
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* Live Preview shows both the settings on the page (including unsaved edits) and what the
  engine executes right now (new preview endpoint, live price, effective sensitivity):
  formula pips, the move the 5-decimal quote actually shows (one-quote-tick floor noted),
  price before → after, BUY/SELL toggle.
* Reference Amount and Reference Pips are editable (they anchor the curve); the banner
  states the exact formula; saves are pushed to the engine immediately.
* Per-round override input is clamped to 1–10 and the toggle follows the automatic clear
  at round end (polled).
* Live Trade Log: formula vs actual per real trade with a mismatch marker, round total
  measured on the price (start → now), real / NPC / other split, trade counts, the
  sensitivity in force.
* Change-log Search, Date Range and Field filters now query the server (the date range
  did nothing before, and search/field only filtered the current page); CURVE and
  REFERENCE options added.
* Price Movement Audit: Pass/Fail filter and the metrics come from the server for the
  whole period; the MULTIPLIER column shows the Market Sensitivity multiplier that priced
  the round (it showed the event multiplier) with a marker when a per-round override was
  active.

